data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Write the compute-bound test as `2 * params * B * bandwidth >= peak * (weights + B * per_sequence)`, where\n`per_sequence = (context + 1) * kv`. Both sides are linear in `B`, so move the `B` terms to one side. The result\nis `B * slope >= needed`, with `slope = 2 * params * bandwidth - peak * per_sequence` and\n`needed = peak * weights`. A slope that is not positive can never satisfy it."},"hints_note":null}

